{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/reflectionprobe"]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"ReflectionProbe","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Captures its surroundings as a cubemap, and stores versions of it with increasing levels of blur to simulate different material roughnesses."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is used to create high-quality reflections at a low performance cost (when "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/updateMode-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/UpdateMode-swift.enum\/once","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe"},{"type":"text","text":"s can be blended together and with the rest of the scene smoothly. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"s can also be combined with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI"},{"text":", SDFGI (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Environment\/sdfgiEnabled","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") and screen-space reflections ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Environment\/ssrEnabled"},{"type":"text","text":") to get more accurate reflections in specific areas. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"s render all objects within their "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/cullMask","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so updating them can be quite expensive. It is best to update them once with the important static objects and then leave them as-is."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unlike "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VoxelGI"},{"text":" and SDFGI, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe","isActive":true},{"text":"s only source their environment from a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/WorldEnvironment","isActive":true},{"text":" node. If you specify an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Environment","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" resource within a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Camera3D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" node, it will be ignored by the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". This can lead to incorrect lighting within the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reflection probes are only supported in the Forward+ and Mobile rendering methods, not Compatibility. When using the Mobile rendering method, only 8 reflection probes can be displayed on each mesh resource. Attempting to display more than 8 reflection probes on a single mesh resource will result in reflection probes flickering in and out as the camera moves.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When using the Mobile rendering method, reflection probes will only correctly affect meshes whose visibility AABB intersects with the reflection probe’s AABB. If using a shader to deform the mesh in a way that makes it go outside its AABB, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GeometryInstance3D\/extraCullMargin"},{"type":"text","text":" must be increased on the mesh. Otherwise, the reflection probe may not be visible on the mesh."}]}],"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/ambientColor","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/ambientColorEnergy","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/ambientMode-swift.property","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/blendDistance","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/boxProjection","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/cullMask","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/enableShadows","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/intensity","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/interior","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/maxDistance","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\